  "summary": "A guest opinion in Colorado Boulevard urges Pasadena to end its Flock ALPR program, citing 61 cameras costing nearly $1 million, ICE data-sharing concerns, and a 2019 state audit finding PPD failed to protect driver privacy. The DeFlock Pasadena campaign demands the city cancel its Flock contract as the City Council prepares to debate the program.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Since September of 2023, the Pasadena Police Department (PPD) has purchased and installed 61 Flock cameras at a cost nearing $1 million",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "A 2019 California state audit found PPD failed to protect the privacy of California drivers; reporting found PPD historically shared ALPR information with ICE.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "DeFlock Pasadena demands that the City: Disable and remove all Flock Safety's ALPRs in and around Pasadena; Commit to canceling the contract with Flock",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
